# ============================================================================
# WolfPack-DFT — .gitignore
# Tracked: the scripts (*.sh, *.py), the wolfpack_plot/ package, and the docs
# (*.md). Everything below is local, generated, or environment-specific.
# ============================================================================

# --- Python bytecode / caches ----------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Packaging / build artifacts -------------------------------------------
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# --- Virtual environments --------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
.conda/

# --- Editor / OS cruft -----------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Backups / scratch -----------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp
Readme.md.bak

# ============================================================================
# VASP run data & tool output — these are produced INSIDE calculation folders
# (and by the test scripts). Ignored so a calc dropped in the repo for testing
# is never committed. If you ever add small example/test data on purpose,
# force-add it:  git add -f path/to/fixture
# ============================================================================

# --- VASP input/output files -----------------------------------------------
WAVECAR
CHGCAR
CHG
CONTCAR
DOSCAR
EIGENVAL
IBZKPT
OSZICAR
OUTCAR
PCDAT
PROCAR
PROOUT
REPORT
vasprun.xml
vaspout.h5
XDATCAR
WAVEDER
LOCPOT
ELFCAR
TMPCAR
HILLSPOT
PENALTYPOT
*.tmp
dryrun_OUTCAR

# --- SLURM / job logs ------------------------------------------------------
slurm-*.out
*.out
*.err
vasp_dryrun_*.out
vasp_dryrun_*.err
vasp_test-*.out
vasp_test-*.err

# --- Toolkit-generated outputs ---------------------------------------------
Plots/
*.fig.pkl
*analysis_report.txt
# isolated benchmark run dirs created by vasp-test:
vasp_test_*/
# occupations table written by collect-u-data:
U_data.dat
# hidden pipeline state / intermediates (dry-run OUTCAR, state.env, job logs):
.wolfpack/
# combined pipeline report:
report.out
# production SLURM script written by vasp-recommend-slurm / updated by vasp-test:
slurm.sh
# legacy names (older versions wrote these):
slurm_job.sh
slurm_job_*.sh
INCAR.parallel
# self-contained job scripts rendered by vasp-dry-run / vasp-test:
slurm_dryrun.sh
slurm_vasptest.sh

# --- Stray figure/data files in the repo root ------------------------------
/*.png
/*.pdf
/*.svg
/*.csv

# ============================================================================
# Test data -- NEVER versioned, in EITHER repo.
# Test/ holds real VASP calculations. Two independent reasons to keep all of it
# out, not just selected file types:
#   * POTCARs are licensed. Their own header says
#       COPYR = ... regulated by the VASP license agreement
#     so redistributing them is a licence violation, and the public repo is the
#     kind of place that gets a repo taken down.
#   * The rest is unpublished research (structures, parameters, results), which
#     should be published by its authors, not leaked by a toolkit commit.
# Whole tree, at any depth, plus the licensed/bulky VASP files anywhere else.
# ============================================================================
Test/
**/Test/
POTCAR
**/POTCAR
POTCAR.spin
WAVECAR.chi
WAVEDER
QP_audit.png

# Stray file produced by a shell redirect typo (a memory figure used as a name):
554308
